  "notes": "CULTURAL IMPORTANCE:\nThis verb is central to Japanese high-context communication. The ability to {察|さっ}する is highly valued in Japanese culture, where direct expression can be avoided in favor of implicit communication.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {空気|くうき}を{読|よ}む (to read the atmosphere)\n- {行間|ぎょうかん}を{読|よ}む (to read between the lines)\n- {言|い}わなくても{分|わ}かる (to understand without being told)\n\nFORMAL EXPRESSION:\n「ご{心中|しんちゅう}{察|さっ}します」is a polite way to express sympathy.",
